// The rules of chess as a library: the pieces, the board's game state, the settled-board judge (captures,
// promotion, castling, en passant, check, the 75-move rule and repetition), the move door (`chessInputOf`, which the
// console's and a replay's moves and a seated player's put-downs share) and a one-ply computer opponent searching
// the same rules. One set of rules plays every game of a world at once, as the patience games do (klondike.puck): a
// game is a station's place in the world's list (`$member` in every rule), each rule sweeps the games
// (`forEach: gameStationOf`, one cell a game) or every game's pieces (`forEach: chessPieceCodeOf`, `$each` a piece),
// and each game's state is the member at its place of a family of rows (`chessTurn[$member]`, `chessMoveOf[$member].from`,
// `chessBoard[$member]`), so a move at one game wakes and costs that game's bindings alone, and each game's computer
// search judges its own game's bindings alone (`chessSearch`, `member:`). A world imports it and expands each template
// where its rows belong, in the order the game stations do (the rules run in document order):
//
//   import "../games/chess"
//   state {
//     enum PieceKind { None Pawn Knight Bishop Rook Queen King }
//     enum MoveKind { Illegal Quiet Capture EnPassant Castle }
//     enum TurnColor { White Black }
//     chessBoardGrids(count: 1, cellSize: 0.2, origin: [-0.8, 1.25, -0.8], band: 0.3)
//     world { chessGameState(keys: [map(range(0, 32), k => $"piece{k}")], settleTicks: 9) }
//   }
//   chessSearch(name: "chessAI", index: 0)
//   chessJudge(settleTicks: 9)
//   chessComputer(settleTicks: 9)
//   chessMoveDoor(settleTicks: 9)
//   chessMoveDone()
//   chessPutDown(settleTicks: 9)
//   chessPutJudged()
//   chessPutSettled()
//
// A world whose board is drawn rather than stood with pieces passes `digital: true` to the judge: its
// pieces are their cells alone and the board is always at rest. A world whose pieces are bodies (a game station's
// holodeck, chess-station.puck) leaves the judge physical: each piece's cell is read from where its body settled, once
// the board has rested and nothing holds the game (`chessHold`). Either may start its pieces on their squares
// (`chessGameState(placed: true)`), and pass `restoresCells: true` to the put-down's judgement, so an arrangement judged
// illegal is put back by writing its cells (a holodeck then stands its bodies where the cells say). Either may also
// expand `chessFreshGame()`, the door (`chessFreshOf[$member].request`) that sets every piece back and starts the game
// afresh. Each game's search job is its own (`chessSearch`), named by the world.
//
// The world declares the three vocabularies itself, each on its own lines as above: the compiler folds an enum's
// members only from declarations the compiled source spells, so a template cannot carry them, and declaring them
// keeps their names readable to every document built on the table.
//
// A world of physical pieces owns everything physical: each game's 32 piece placements, named by the keys it gives its
// game's pieces (`chessGameState(keys:)`, piece n starting on `initialPieceCodes[n]`'s square), their bodies and looks,
// each game's board placement whose `board` block anchors its topology (`occupancy` and `topology` both
// `chessBoard<i>`, game i's member of the `chessBoard` family over its own grid of the same name), and posing the pieces
// a move door relocates. A `chessBoard<i>` grid is cell = 8 * row + column, its rows running +Z and its columns +X; a rank
// is a row (rank 1 on the -Z side, White's) and a file runs the other way, column = 7 - file. The judge reads the
// arrangement once the game's pieces have rested `settleTicks` ticks. A game station's holodeck chess
// (chess-station.puck) is the worked example.

// The back rank's piece codes from file a to h (rook, knight, bishop, queen, king, bishop, knight, rook), White
// positive and Black negative; the board's cells hold them by column.
let backRankCodes = [4, 2, 3, 5, 6, 3, 2, 4]
let backRankByColumn = map(range(0, 8), column => backRankCodes[7 - column])
let initialBoard = concat(
  backRankByColumn,
  map(range(0, 8), i => 1),
  map(range(0, 32), i => 0),
  map(range(0, 8), i => -1),
  map(backRankByColumn, code => -code)
)
// Each piece's starting cell: piece n stands on file n % 8 of rank 0, 1, 6 or 7 by its eighth, at column 7 - file.
let initialPieceCells = map(range(0, 32), i => 8 * [0, 1, 6, 7][floor(i / 8)] + 7 - i % 8)
let initialPieceCodes = concat(
  backRankCodes,
  map(range(0, 8), i => 1),
  map(range(0, 8), i => -1),
  map(backRankCodes, code => -code)
)

// Where each piece could move, as (column, row) steps on the `chessBoard` grid: the search tries only these cells and
// the judging rules still decide every move. A pawn steps, double-steps and takes (en passant included) forward, the
// king steps and castles two columns, and the bishop, rook and queen slide to the edge or the first piece. Each side's
// patterns apply only on its own turn, so the side not to move offers no candidate.
let orthogonalSteps = [[1, 0], [-1, 0], [0, 1], [0, -1]]
let diagonalSteps = [[1, 1], [1, -1], [-1, 1], [-1, -1]]
let knightSteps = [[1, 2], [2, 1], [2, -1], [1, -2], [-1, -2], [-2, -1], [-2, 1], [-1, 2]]
let kingSteps = concat(orthogonalSteps, diagonalSteps, [[2, 0], [-2, 0]])
let chessMoves = concat(
  map(
    [1, -1],
    sign => { codes [sign], turn: (1 - sign) / 2, offsets [[0, sign], [0, 2 * sign], [1, sign], [-1, sign]] }
  ),
  map([1, -1], sign => { codes [2 * sign], turn: (1 - sign) / 2, offsets: knightSteps }),
  map([1, -1], sign => { codes [3 * sign, 5 * sign], turn: (1 - sign) / 2, offsets: diagonalSteps, range: 0 }),
  map([1, -1], sign => { codes [4 * sign, 5 * sign], turn: (1 - sign) / 2, offsets: orthogonalSteps, range: 0 }),
  map([1, -1], sign => { codes [6 * sign], turn: (1 - sign) / 2, offsets: kingSteps })
)

// Whether the pawn of the side to move on `source` can take en passant: it stands on the victim's rank, and no rook,
// bishop or queen of the other side reaches the king along a ray over `occupied`, the occupancy once it has taken. Read
// inside `tabletop-history-en-passant`, over its locals (`victim`, `sign`, `kingMask`, `rooks`, `bishops`); a source off
// the board reads no square.
function chessEnPassantFrom(source, occupied) = ((source >= 0) and
  (source < 64) and
  ((source / 8) == (victim / 8)) and
  (chessBoard[$member][source] == sign) and
  (rooks &
    (boardSlide(kingMask, occupied, chessBoard0, N) |
      boardSlide(kingMask, occupied, chessBoard0, S) |
      boardSlide(kingMask, occupied, chessBoard0, E) |
      boardSlide(kingMask, occupied, chessBoard0, W)) ==
    0) and
  (bishops &
    (boardSlide(kingMask, occupied, chessBoard0, NE) |
      boardSlide(kingMask, occupied, chessBoard0, SE) |
      boardSlide(kingMask, occupied, chessBoard0, SW) |
      boardSlide(kingMask, occupied, chessBoard0, NW)) ==
    0))

// Every game's board grid, expanded inside the world's `state` block: game i's `chessBoard<i>`, `cellSize` one square in
// metres, `origin` the grid's corner in the frame of the placement that anchors it and `band` how far above a square a
// piece still counts as standing on it; and the families of each game's boards (`chessBoard`, `chessLastLegal`) and
// repetition tallies (`chessPositionCounts`) whose members chessGameState declares.
template chessBoardGrids(count, cellSize, origin, band) {
  lattices [
    for index in range(0, count) {
      grid(
        band: band,
        cellSize: cellSize,
        depth: 8,
        directions: [
          {
            name: "N"
            x: 0
            y: -1
            z: 0
          }
          {
            name: "NE"
            x: 1
            y: -1
            z: 0
          }
          {
            name: "E"
            x: 1
            y: 0
            z: 0
          }
          {
            name: "SE"
            x: 1
            y: 1
            z: 0
          }
          {
            name: "S"
            x: 0
            y: 1
            z: 0
          }
          {
            name: "SW"
            x: -1
            y: 1
            z: 0
          }
          {
            name: "W"
            x: -1
            y: 0
            z: 0
          }
          {
            name: "NW"
            x: -1
            y: -1
            z: 0
          }
        ],
        name: $"chessBoard{index}",
        origin: origin,
        width: 8,
        wrap: None
      )
    }
  ]
  families [
    { name: "chessBoard", size: count }
    { name: "chessLastLegal", size: count }
    { name: "chessPositionCounts", size: count }
  ]
}

// Every game's state rows, expanded inside the world's `state.world` block: `keys` lists each game's 32 piece keys in
// piece order (the names of its piece placements), game i at place i. With `placed` the pieces start on their squares (a
// drawn board, or a holodeck that stands its bodies where the cells say); without it they are read off the board once it
// first rests.
template chessGameState(keys, settleTicks, placed = false) {
  let count = length(keys)

  // Each game's pieces, keyed by its own keys: the cell each stands on (-1 off the board) and its code, the board they
  // make (its inverse), and what the start, the computer and a put-down hold of them.
  table chessPieceCellOf[count] as g capacity(32) bounds(-1..63) {
    for k in range(0, 32) {
      [keys[g][k]] = (placed ? initialPieceCells[k] : -1)
    }
  }
  table chessPieceCodeOf[count] as g capacity(32) bounds(-6..6) {
    for k in range(0, 32) {
      [keys[g][k]] = initialPieceCodes[k]
    }
  }
  for g in range(0, count) {
    row {
      capacity: 64
      domain: cellsOf(topology: $"chessBoard{g}")
      kind: "Int"
      max: 6
      min: -6
      name: $"chessBoard{g}"
      inverse {
        tokens: $"chessPieceCellOf{g}"
        codes: $"chessPieceCodeOf{g}"
      }
    }
  }
  for g in range(0, count) {
    row {
      capacity: 64
      cells: map(initialBoard, (code, i) => { key: $"{i}", value: code })
      domain: cellsOf(topology: $"chessBoard{g}")
      kind: "Int"
      max: 6
      min: -6
      name: $"chessLastLegal{g}"
    }
  }
  // How many times each position of the current stretch of reversible play has stood, by position key. The 75-move
  // limit ends play after 150 reversible plies, so a stretch holds at most 151 positions, the initial one included.
  for g in range(0, count) {
    row {
      name: $"chessPositionCounts{g}"
      kind: "Int"
      domain: tally(capacity: 151)
    }
  }
  table chessPieceStartCellOf[count] as g capacity(32) {
    for k in range(0, 32) {
      [keys[g][k]] = initialPieceCells[k]
    }
  }
  table chessPieceStartCodeOf[count] as g capacity(32) {
    for k in range(0, 32) {
      [keys[g][k]] = initialPieceCodes[k]
    }
  }
  table chessAiBeforeOf[count] as g capacity(32) {
    for k in range(0, 32) {
      [keys[g][k]] = -1
    }
  }
  // What a put-down is judged against: every piece's cell and code the tick it was made.
  table chessPutBeforeOf[count] as g capacity(32) bounds(-1..63) {
    for k in range(0, 32) {
      [keys[g][k]] = -1
    }
  }
  table chessPutBeforeCodeOf[count] as g capacity(32) bounds(-6..6) {
    for k in range(0, 32) {
      [keys[g][k]] = initialPieceCodes[k]
    }
  }

  // The move door (`chessInputOf`), the computer's working cells and its answer, the candidate move the judge reads, and
  // each side's pending promotion, check and the castling transits.
  table chessInputOf[count] capacity(4) {
    from = -1
    to = -1
    request = 0
    accepted = 0
  }
  table chessAiOf[count] capacity(5) {
    metadata = -1
    pending = 0
    from = -1
    to = -1
    mover = 0
  }
  slot chessAiEvaluation[count] = 0
  table chessAiBestOf[count] capacity(4) {
    token = -1
    to = -1
    score = 0
    revision = -1
  }
  slot chessAiSide[count] = 1 bounds(-1..1)
  slot chessAiEnabled[count] = 0 bounds(0..1)
  slot chessAiRevision[count] = 0
  table chessMoveOf[count] capacity(5) bounds(-6..63) {
    captured = 0
    from = -1
    kind = 0
    mover = 0
    to = -1
  }
  table chessPromotionPendingOf[count] capacity(2) bounds(-1..63) {
    "0" = -1
    "1" = -1
  }
  table chessInCheckOf[count] capacity(2) bounds(0..1) {
    "0" = 0
    "1" = 0
  }
  table chessPreviousInCheckOf[count] capacity(2) bounds(0..1) {
    "0" = 0
    "1" = 0
  }
  table chessCastleTransitOf[count] capacity(4) bounds(0..1) {
    wk = 0
    wq = 0
    bk = 0
    bq = 0
  }

  slot chessTurn[count] = 0 bounds(0..1)
  slot chessVerdict[count] = 1 bounds(0..1)
  slot chessIllegalCount[count] = 0 bounds(0..50400)
  slot chessSettleHold[count] = 0 bounds(0..settleTicks)
  slot chessGameStarted[count] = 0 bounds(0..1)
  slot chessEnPassantTarget[count] = -1 bounds(-1..63)
  slot chessRepetitionEnPassant[count] = -1 bounds(-1..63)
  slot chessHistoryPending[count] = 0 bounds(0..1)
  slot chessHistoryReset[count] = 0 bounds(0..1)
  slot chessHistoryLength[count] = 0 bounds(0..151)
  slot chessHalfmoveClock[count] = 0 bounds(0..150)
  slot chessRepetitionCount[count] = 0 bounds(0..76)
  slot chessShapeLegal[count] = 0 bounds(0..1)
  slot chessCastleLegal[count] = 0 bounds(0..1)
  slot chessCastleRights[count] = 0 bounds(0..15)
  slot chessBoardMismatch[count] = 0 bounds(0..64)
  slot chessBoardChanged[count] = 0 bounds(0..64)
  slot chessBoardCollisions[count] = 0 bounds(0..64)

  // Whether the board's pieces rest (a drawn board always does), and whether the computer and the doors hold off (a
  // table's demonstration sets it while it plays).
  slot chessRested[count] = 1 bounds(0..1)
  slot chessHold[count] = 0 bounds(0..1)

  // The display door (chessPutDown): the squares a move leaves and lands on and the request a presentation of the game
  // away from its board posts, and whether a seat plays the game there now. While a physical table's seated player holds
  // a piece up (`chessGrip`, which such a table keeps), the door takes no move: the board is the player's until the
  // piece is down.
  table chessPutOf[count] capacity(3) {
    from = -1
    to = -1
    request = 0
  }
  slot chessSeated[count] = 0 bounds(0..1)
  slot chessGrip[count] = 0 bounds(0..1)

  // The fresh-game door (chessFreshGame), and a put-down awaiting its verdict (`judging`) and the arrangement being put
  // back this tick (`revert`).
  table chessFreshOf[count] capacity(1) {
    request = 0
  }
  table chessPutDownOf[count] capacity(2) {
    judging = 0
    revert = 0
  }
}

// Game `index`'s computer opponent, searching the same rules over its own game's rows alone: its judge binds every rule
// to the game's member (`member`), so a move at another game never restarts it. A job's name is the search section's own.
template chessSearch(name, index) {
  search {
    jobs [
      {
        name: name
        member: index
        tokens: $"chessPieceCellOf{index}"
        board: $"chessBoard{index}"
        turn: $"chessTurn{index}"
        verdict: $"chessVerdict{index}"
        enabled: $"chessAiEnabled{index}"
        revision: $"chessAiRevision{index}"
        depth: 1
        best: $"chessAiBestOf{index}"
        shapes [
          relocate(displace: true, codes: $"chessPieceCodeOf{index}", moves: chessMoves)
        ]
        // The score is from the side that just moved. One ply, automatic queen
        // promotion, material first, then central occupation and pawn progress.
        score: (2 * $"chessTurn{index}" - 1) * $"chessAiEvaluation{index}"
      }
    ]
  }
}

// The settled-board judge: once a game's board has rested `settleTicks` ticks, the rules read the arrangement off the
// board and judge it against the last legal position. A physical table's board rests while its game's piece bodies do,
// and each piece's cell is read from where its body settled; a drawn board (`digital`) always rests and its cells are its
// pieces.
template chessJudge(settleTicks, digital = false) {
  pattern chessRayEmpty: Int {
    symbols {
      vacant = 0
    }
    match: vacant*
  }

  // A held game is never read off its bodies: a holodeck releases them while it shows another game.
  if digital {} else {
    rule "tabletop-rested" {
      local rested = physics(quiescent, chessPieceCodeOf[$member]) and chessHold[$member] == 0
      when chessRested[$member] != rested
      mode: Level
      forEach: gameStationOf
      chessRested[$member] = rested
    }
  }

  rule "tabletop-settle-hold-advance" {
    when chessRested[$member] == 1 and chessSettleHold[$member] < settleTicks
    mode: Level
    forEach: gameStationOf
    chessSettleHold[$member] += 1
  }

  rule "tabletop-settle-hold-reset" {
    when chessRested[$member] != 1
    mode: Level
    forEach: gameStationOf
    chessSettleHold[$member] = 0
  }

  // Each piece is read as its body comes to rest: the square under an upright body, or none for a body knocked over. The
  // gate is the body's own rest, so a settle reads only the pieces disturbed since they last rested, never a body that
  // did not move, and never one absent (released, which never rests) or held (a held game's bodies stand for none).
  // Every disturbed body rests by the tick the board does, so each cell is read before the settled board is judged.
  if digital {} else {
    rule "tabletop-derive-cell" {
      when fact(placement, $each, Resting)
      mode: Edge
      forEach: chessPieceCodeOf
      if chessHold[$member] == 0 {
        if upright(placement, $each) >= 0.5 {
          chessPieceCellOf[$member][$each] = board(cellOf, chessBoard[$member], placement, $each)
        } else {
          chessPieceCellOf[$member][$each] = -1
        }
      }
    }
  }

  // Keep the established rule names while sharing the settled-board gate and edge mode.
  rules "" when chessSettleHold[$member] == settleTicks {
    mode: "Edge"
    rule "tabletop-board-collisions" {
      forEach: gameStationOf
      chessBoardCollisions[$member] = count(chessPieceCellOf[$member], atLeast: 0, atMost: 63) + setBitCount(
        board(mask, chessBoard[$member], 0, 0)
      ) - 64
    }

    rule "tabletop-game-start-snapshot" {
      when chessGameStarted[$member] == 0 and chessBoardCollisions[$member] == 0
      forEach: gameStationOf
      transform boardCombine(left: chessBoard[$member], operation: Copy, row: chessLastLegal[$member])
    }

    rule "tabletop-candidate-cells" {
      local turn = chessTurn[$member]
      local ownBefore = turn == 0 ? board(mask, chessLastLegal[$member], 1, 6) : board(mask, chessLastLegal[$member], -6, -1)
      local ownAfter = turn == 0 ? board(mask, chessBoard[$member], 1, 6) : board(mask, chessBoard[$member], -6, -1)
      local sources = ownBefore & ~(board(mask, chessBoard[$member], 1, 6) | board(mask, chessBoard[$member], -6, -1))
      local destinations = ownAfter & ~ownBefore
      local kingBefore = turn == 0 ? board(mask, chessLastLegal[$member], 6, 6) : board(mask, chessLastLegal[$member], -6, -6)
      local kingAfter = turn == 0 ? board(mask, chessBoard[$member], 6, 6) : board(mask, chessBoard[$member], -6, -6)
      local target = sources & kingBefore != 0 ? destinations & kingAfter : destinations
      forEach: gameStationOf
      chessMoveOf[$member].from = sources == 0 ? -1 : trailingZeroCount(sources & kingBefore != 0 ? sources & kingBefore : sources)
      chessMoveOf[$member].to = target == 0 ? -1 : trailingZeroCount(target)
    }

    rule "tabletop-candidate-move" {
      local turn = chessTurn[$member]
      local from = chessMoveOf[$member].from
      local to = chessMoveOf[$member].to
      local mover = chessLastLegal[$member][from]
      local kind = (
        (from < 0) or (to < 0) or (to > 63) ? MoveKind.Illegal :
        (absolute(mover) == PieceKind.King) and (absolute(to - from) == 2) ? MoveKind.Castle :
        (absolute(mover) == PieceKind.Pawn) and ((from ^ to) & 7 != 0) and (chessLastLegal[$member][to] == 0) ?
          MoveKind.EnPassant :
        chessLastLegal[$member][to] != 0 ? MoveKind.Capture :
        MoveKind.Quiet
      )
      forEach: gameStationOf
      chessMoveOf[$member].mover = mover
      chessMoveOf[$member].kind = kind
      chessMoveOf[$member].captured = kind == MoveKind.EnPassant ? chessLastLegal[$member][to - 8 * (1 - 2 * turn)] : chessLastLegal[$member][to]
    }

    // Search relocates the primary token; these hypothetical-only rules complete
    // the compound move before the same validator used for physical play judges it. Each names one piece.
    rule "tabletop-search-en-passant" {
      when search(ply) > 0 and chessMoveOf[$member].kind == MoveKind.EnPassant and chessMoveOf[$member].to == chessEnPassantTarget[$member] and chessPieceCellOf[$member][$each] == (
          chessMoveOf[$member].to - 8 * (1 - 2 * chessTurn[$member])
        )
      forEach: chessPieceCodeOf
      maxFirings: 1
      chessPieceCellOf[$member][$each] = -1
    }

    rule "tabletop-search-castle" {
      when search(ply) > 0 and chessMoveOf[$member].kind == MoveKind.Castle and chessPieceCellOf[$member][$each] == (
          (chessMoveOf[$member].from & 56) + (chessMoveOf[$member].to > chessMoveOf[$member].from ? 7 : 0)
        ) and chessPieceCodeOf[$member][$each] == (4 * (1 - 2 * chessTurn[$member]))
      forEach: chessPieceCodeOf
      maxFirings: 1
      chessPieceCellOf[$member][$each] = chessMoveOf[$member].from + chessMoveOf[$member].to >> 1
    }

    rule "tabletop-search-promotion" {
      when (search(ply) > 0 and
        absolute(chessMoveOf[$member].mover) == PieceKind.Pawn and
        chessPieceCellOf[$member][$each] == chessMoveOf[$member].to and
        (chessMoveOf[$member].to / 8) == (chessTurn[$member] == TurnColor.White ? 7 : 0))
      forEach: chessPieceCodeOf
      maxFirings: 1
      chessPieceCodeOf[$member][$each] = PieceKind.Queen * (1 - 2 * chessTurn[$member])
    }

    rule "tabletop-candidate-match" {
      local changed = (
        (board(mask, chessBoard[$member], -3, -2) | board(mask, chessBoard[$member], 1, 2) | board(mask, chessBoard[$member], 5, 6)) ^
          (board(mask, chessLastLegal[$member], -3, -2) | board(mask, chessLastLegal[$member], 1, 2) | board(mask, chessLastLegal[$member], 5, 6)) |
        (board(mask, chessBoard[$member], -5, -3) | board(mask, chessBoard[$member], 2, 5)) ^
          (board(mask, chessLastLegal[$member], -5, -3) | board(mask, chessLastLegal[$member], 2, 5)) |
        board(mask, chessBoard[$member], -4, 3) ^ board(mask, chessLastLegal[$member], -4, 3) |
        board(mask, chessBoard[$member], 0, 7) ^ board(mask, chessLastLegal[$member], 0, 7)
      )
      local from = chessMoveOf[$member].from
      local to = chessMoveOf[$member].to
      local kind = chessMoveOf[$member].kind
      local mover = chessMoveOf[$member].mover
      local turn = chessTurn[$member]
      local sign = 1 - 2 * turn
      local clear = (
        kind == MoveKind.Castle ? (from & 56) + (to > from ? 7 : 0) :
        kind == MoveKind.EnPassant ? to - 8 * sign :
        -1
      )
      local rook = kind == MoveKind.Castle ? from + to >> 1 : -1
      local clearUnique = (clear >= 0) and (clear < 64) and (clear != from) and (clear != to)
      local rookUnique = (rook >= 0) and (rook < 64) and (rook != from) and (rook != to) and (rook != clear)
      local footprint = (
        (from >= 0) * (1 << maximum(from, 0)) |
        (to >= 0) * (1 << maximum(to, 0)) |
        clearUnique * (1 << clamp(clear, 0, 63)) |
        rookUnique * (1 << clamp(rook, 0, 63))
      )
      local landed = (
        (absolute(mover) == PieceKind.Pawn) and (to / 8 == (turn == TurnColor.White ? 7 : 0)) ? chessBoard[$member][to] :
        mover
      )
      forEach: gameStationOf
      chessBoardMismatch[$member] = (
        setBitCount(changed & ~(footprint)) +
        (from >= 0) * (chessBoard[$member][from] != 0) +
        (to >= 0) * (chessBoard[$member][to] != landed) +
        clearUnique * (chessBoard[$member][clear] != 0) +
        rookUnique * (chessBoard[$member][rook] != 4 * sign)
      )
      chessBoardChanged[$member] = setBitCount(changed)
    }

    // The square a castling king passes over, f1 (cell 2) or d1 (cell 4), or f8 (58) or d8 (60), attacked by a pawn,
    // knight or king standing on the mask's cells or by a slider; kingside runs toward column 0.
    rule "tabletop-castle-transit-attacked" {
      when chessMoveOf[$member].kind == MoveKind.Castle
      forEach: gameStationOf
      chessCastleTransitOf[$member].wk = 0
      chessCastleTransitOf[$member].wq = 0
      chessCastleTransitOf[$member].bk = 0
      chessCastleTransitOf[$member].bq = 0
      if chessTurn[$member] == TurnColor.White and chessMoveOf[$member].to < chessMoveOf[$member].from {
        chessCastleTransitOf[$member].wk = (
          (
            (board(mask, chessLastLegal[$member], -1, -1) & 2560 != 0) or
            (board(mask, chessLastLegal[$member], -2, -2) & 659712 != 0) or
            (board(mask, chessLastLegal[$member], -6, -6) & 3594 != 0)
          ) |
          board(attacks, chessLastLegal[$member], -5, -4, "N,S,E,W")[2] |
          board(attacks, chessLastLegal[$member], -3, -3, "NE,SE,SW,NW")[2] |
          board(attacks, chessLastLegal[$member], -5, -5, "NE,SE,SW,NW")[2]
        )
      } else if chessTurn[$member] == TurnColor.White {
        chessCastleTransitOf[$member].wq = (
          (
            (board(mask, chessLastLegal[$member], -1, -1) & 10240 != 0) or
            (board(mask, chessLastLegal[$member], -2, -2) & 2638848 != 0) or
            (board(mask, chessLastLegal[$member], -6, -6) & 14376 != 0)
          ) |
          board(attacks, chessLastLegal[$member], -5, -4, "N,S,E,W")[4] |
          board(attacks, chessLastLegal[$member], -3, -3, "NE,SE,SW,NW")[4] |
          board(attacks, chessLastLegal[$member], -5, -5, "NE,SE,SW,NW")[4]
        )
      } else if chessMoveOf[$member].to < chessMoveOf[$member].from {
        chessCastleTransitOf[$member].bk = (
          (
            (board(mask, chessLastLegal[$member], 1, 1) & byteSwap(2560) != 0) or
            (board(mask, chessLastLegal[$member], 2, 2) & byteSwap(659712) != 0) or
            (board(mask, chessLastLegal[$member], 6, 6) & byteSwap(3594) != 0)
          ) |
          board(attacks, chessLastLegal[$member], 4, 5, "N,S,E,W")[58] |
          board(attacks, chessLastLegal[$member], 3, 3, "NE,SE,SW,NW")[58] |
          board(attacks, chessLastLegal[$member], 5, 5, "NE,SE,SW,NW")[58]
        )
      } else {
        chessCastleTransitOf[$member].bq = (
          (
            (board(mask, chessLastLegal[$member], 1, 1) & byteSwap(10240) != 0) or
            (board(mask, chessLastLegal[$member], 2, 2) & byteSwap(2638848) != 0) or
            (board(mask, chessLastLegal[$member], 6, 6) & byteSwap(14376) != 0)
          ) |
          board(attacks, chessLastLegal[$member], 4, 5, "N,S,E,W")[60] |
          board(attacks, chessLastLegal[$member], 3, 3, "NE,SE,SW,NW")[60] |
          board(attacks, chessLastLegal[$member], 5, 5, "NE,SE,SW,NW")[60]
        )
      }
    }

    // The king starts in column 3; a rising column (direction 1) castles queenside with the column-7 rook, a falling one
    // kingside with the column-0 rook. A right's bit names its rook's column: 1 column 0, 2 column 7, Black's two above.
    rule "tabletop-castle-legal" {
      local turn = chessTurn[$member]
      local from = chessMoveOf[$member].from
      local to = chessMoveOf[$member].to
      local sign = 1 - 2 * turn
      local home = 3 + 56 * turn
      local direction = to > from ? 1 : -1
      local rook = home + (direction == 1 ? 4 : -3)
      local right = (direction == 1 ? 2 : 1) << 2 * turn
      local attacked = (
        turn == TurnColor.White ? direction == 1 ? chessCastleTransitOf[$member].wq :
        chessCastleTransitOf[$member].wk :
        direction == 1 ? chessCastleTransitOf[$member].bq :
        chessCastleTransitOf[$member].bk
      )
      forEach: gameStationOf
      chessCastleLegal[$member] = 0
      if chessMoveOf[$member].kind == MoveKind.Castle {
        chessCastleLegal[$member] = (
          (from == home) and
          (to == home + 2 * direction) and
          (chessCastleRights[$member] & right == 0) and
          (chessLastLegal[$member][rook] == PieceKind.Rook * sign) and
          (
            (
              direction == 1 ? match(chessRayEmpty, chessLastLegal[$member], E, cell)[from] :
              match(chessRayEmpty, chessLastLegal[$member], W, cell)[from]
            ) == rook
          ) and
          (chessPreviousInCheckOf[$member][turn] == 0) and
          (attacked == 0)
        )
      }
    }

    rule "tabletop-shape-final" {
      local turn = chessTurn[$member]
      local from = chessMoveOf[$member].from
      local to = chessMoveOf[$member].to
      local kind = chessMoveOf[$member].kind
      local piece = absolute(chessMoveOf[$member].mover)
      local dx = absolute(to % 8 - from % 8)
      local dy = (to / 8 - from / 8) * (1 - 2 * turn)
      local middle = from + 8 * (1 - 2 * turn)
      forEach: gameStationOf
      chessShapeLegal[$member] = 0
      if piece == PieceKind.Pawn {
        chessShapeLegal[$member] = (
          (dx == 0) and
            (chessLastLegal[$member][to] == 0) and
            (dy == 1 or (dy == 2) and (from / 8 == (turn == TurnColor.White ? 1 : 6)) and (chessLastLegal[$member][middle] == 0)) or
          (dx == 1) and
            (dy == 1) and
            (
              kind == MoveKind.Capture or
                (kind == MoveKind.EnPassant) and (to == chessEnPassantTarget[$member]) and (chessMoveOf[$member].captured == 2 * turn - 1)
            )
        )
      } else if piece == PieceKind.Knight {
        chessShapeLegal[$member] = dx * absolute(dy) == 2
      } else if piece == PieceKind.King {
        chessShapeLegal[$member] = (maximum(dx, absolute(dy)) == 1) and (kind != MoveKind.Castle) or chessCastleLegal[$member]
      } else {
        if piece == PieceKind.Rook or piece == PieceKind.Queen {
          chessShapeLegal[$member] = any([N, S, E, W], ray => match(chessRayEmpty, chessLastLegal[$member], ray, cell)[to] == from)
        }
        if piece == PieceKind.Bishop or piece == PieceKind.Queen {
          chessShapeLegal[$member] |= any([NE, SE, SW, NW], ray => match(chessRayEmpty, chessLastLegal[$member], ray, cell)[to] == from)
        }
      }
    }

    rule "tabletop-check-white" {
      local kingMask = lowestSetBit(board(mask, chessBoard[$member], 6, 6))
      local kingSquare = kingMask == 0 ? -1 : trailingZeroCount(kingMask)
      local nearFiles = boardShift(kingMask, chessBoard0, E) | boardShift(kingMask, chessBoard0, W)
      local farFiles = (boardShift(nearFiles, chessBoard0, E) | boardShift(nearFiles, chessBoard0, W)) & ~(kingMask)
      local kingBand = kingMask | nearFiles
      local closeHit = (
        boardShift(nearFiles, chessBoard0, S) & board(mask, chessBoard[$member], -1, -1) |
          (kingBand | boardShift(kingBand, chessBoard0, S) | boardShift(kingBand, chessBoard0, N)) &
            board(mask, chessBoard[$member], -6, -6) !=
        0
      )
      local knightHit = (
        (
          boardShift(boardShift(nearFiles, chessBoard0, S), chessBoard0, S) |
          boardShift(boardShift(nearFiles, chessBoard0, N), chessBoard0, N) |
          boardShift(farFiles, chessBoard0, S) |
          boardShift(farFiles, chessBoard0, N)
        ) &
          board(mask, chessBoard[$member], -2, -2) !=
        0
      )
      local slideHit = (
        (kingMask != 0) &
        (
          board(attacks, chessBoard[$member], -5, -4, "N,S,E,W")[kingSquare] |
          board(attacks, chessBoard[$member], -3, -3, "NE,SE,SW,NW")[kingSquare] |
          board(attacks, chessBoard[$member], -5, -5, "NE,SE,SW,NW")[kingSquare]
        )
      )
      forEach: gameStationOf
      chessInCheckOf[$member][0] = closeHit | knightHit | slideHit
    }

    rule "tabletop-check-black" {
      local kingMask = lowestSetBit(board(mask, chessBoard[$member], -6, -6))
      local kingSquare = kingMask == 0 ? -1 : trailingZeroCount(kingMask)
      local nearFiles = boardShift(kingMask, chessBoard0, E) | boardShift(kingMask, chessBoard0, W)
      local farFiles = (boardShift(nearFiles, chessBoard0, E) | boardShift(nearFiles, chessBoard0, W)) & ~(kingMask)
      local kingBand = kingMask | nearFiles
      local closeHit = (
        boardShift(nearFiles, chessBoard0, N) & board(mask, chessBoard[$member], 1, 1) |
          (kingBand | boardShift(kingBand, chessBoard0, S) | boardShift(kingBand, chessBoard0, N)) &
            board(mask, chessBoard[$member], 6, 6) !=
        0
      )
      local knightHit = (
        (
          boardShift(boardShift(nearFiles, chessBoard0, S), chessBoard0, S) |
          boardShift(boardShift(nearFiles, chessBoard0, N), chessBoard0, N) |
          boardShift(farFiles, chessBoard0, S) |
          boardShift(farFiles, chessBoard0, N)
        ) &
          board(mask, chessBoard[$member], 2, 2) !=
        0
      )
      local slideHit = (
        (kingMask != 0) &
        (
          board(attacks, chessBoard[$member], 4, 5, "N,S,E,W")[kingSquare] |
          board(attacks, chessBoard[$member], 3, 3, "NE,SE,SW,NW")[kingSquare] |
          board(attacks, chessBoard[$member], 5, 5, "NE,SE,SW,NW")[kingSquare]
        )
      )
      forEach: gameStationOf
      chessInCheckOf[$member][1] = closeHit | knightHit | slideHit
    }

    rule "tabletop-game-start-check" {
      when chessGameStarted[$member] == 0 and chessBoardCollisions[$member] == 0
      forEach: gameStationOf
      chessPreviousInCheckOf[$member][0] = chessInCheckOf[$member][0]
      chessPreviousInCheckOf[$member][1] = chessInCheckOf[$member][1]
      chessGameStarted[$member] = 1
      chessHistoryPending[$member] = 1
      chessHistoryReset[$member] = 1
    }

    rule "tabletop-verdict" {
      local turn = chessTurn[$member]
      local to = chessMoveOf[$member].to
      local mover = chessMoveOf[$member].mover
      local sign = 1 - 2 * turn
      local promotes = (absolute(mover) == PieceKind.Pawn) and (to / 8 == (turn == TurnColor.White ? 7 : 0))
      local replacement = (
        promotes ? (chessBoard[$member][to] * sign >= PieceKind.Knight) and (chessBoard[$member][to] * sign <= PieceKind.Queen) :
        chessBoard[$member][to] == mover
      )
      local kings = (setBitCount(board(mask, chessBoard[$member], 6, 6)) == 1) and (setBitCount(board(mask, chessBoard[$member], -6, -6)) == 1)
      forEach: gameStationOf
      chessVerdict[$member] = (
        (
          (chessHalfmoveClock[$member] < 150) and
          (chessMoveOf[$member].kind >= MoveKind.Quiet) and
          (chessMoveOf[$member].kind <= MoveKind.Castle) and
          (chessBoardMismatch[$member] == 0) and
          (chessBoardCollisions[$member] == 0) and
          chessShapeLegal[$member]
        ) &
        replacement &
        (mover * sign > 0) &
        (chessMoveOf[$member].captured * sign <= 0) &
        (chessInCheckOf[$member][turn] == 0) &
        kings
      )
      chessPromotionPendingOf[$member][0] = chessBoardChanged[$member] == 0 ? -1 : chessPromotionPendingOf[$member][0]
      chessPromotionPendingOf[$member][1] = chessBoardChanged[$member] == 0 ? -1 : chessPromotionPendingOf[$member][1]
    }

    rule "tabletop-promotion-pending" {
      local turn = chessTurn[$member]
      local to = chessMoveOf[$member].to
      local mover = chessMoveOf[$member].mover
      when chessVerdict[$member] == 0 and (absolute(mover) == PieceKind.Pawn and (to / 8) == (
            turn == TurnColor.White ? 7 : 0
          ) and chessBoard[$member][to] == mover and chessShapeLegal[$member] and chessBoardMismatch[$member] == 0 and chessBoardCollisions[$member] == 0 and chessInCheckOf[$member][turn] == 0 and setBitCount(
            board(mask, chessBoard[$member], 6, 6)
          ) == 1 and setBitCount(board(mask, chessBoard[$member], -6, -6)) == 1)
      forEach: gameStationOf
      chessPromotionPendingOf[$member][turn] = to
    }

    rule "tabletop-advance-turn" {
      local mover = chessMoveOf[$member].mover
      local from = chessMoveOf[$member].from
      local to = chessMoveOf[$member].to
      local lostRooks = (
        board(mask, chessLastLegal[$member], 4, 4) & ~(board(mask, chessBoard[$member], 4, 4)) & 129 |
        board(mask, chessLastLegal[$member], -4, -4) & ~(board(mask, chessBoard[$member], -4, -4)) & 129 << 56
      )
      local lostKings = (
        board(mask, chessLastLegal[$member], 6, 6) & ~(board(mask, chessBoard[$member], 6, 6)) & 1 << 3 |
        board(mask, chessLastLegal[$member], -6, -6) & ~(board(mask, chessBoard[$member], -6, -6)) & 1 << 59
      )
      local lostRights = (
        parallelBitExtract(lostRooks, 129 | 129 << 56) |
        parallelBitDeposit(parallelBitExtract(lostKings, 1 << 3 | 1 << 59), 5) * 3
      )
      when chessVerdict[$member] == 1 and chessMoveOf[$member].kind != MoveKind.Illegal
      forEach: gameStationOf
      transaction {
        // A pawn move, capture or lost castling right makes every earlier position unreachable.
        chessHistoryReset[$member] = (
          (absolute(mover) == PieceKind.Pawn) or (chessMoveOf[$member].captured != 0) or (lostRights & ~((chessCastleRights[$member])) != 0)
        )
        chessHalfmoveClock[$member] = (absolute(mover) == PieceKind.Pawn) or (chessMoveOf[$member].captured != 0) ? 0 : chessHalfmoveClock[$member] + 1
        chessHistoryPending[$member] = 1
        chessCastleRights[$member] |= lostRights
        transform boardCombine(left: chessBoard[$member], operation: Copy, row: chessLastLegal[$member])
        chessPreviousInCheckOf[$member][0] = chessInCheckOf[$member][0]
        chessPreviousInCheckOf[$member][1] = chessInCheckOf[$member][1]
        chessEnPassantTarget[$member] = (
          (absolute(mover) == PieceKind.Pawn) and (absolute(to - from) == 16) ? from + to >> 1 :
          -1
        )
        chessTurn[$member] = 1 - chessTurn[$member]
        chessPromotionPendingOf[$member][0] = -1
        chessPromotionPendingOf[$member][1] = -1
      }
    }

    // A reset starts a new stretch of play: every position of the old one is unreachable.
    rule "tabletop-history-prepare" {
      when chessHistoryPending[$member] == 1
      forEach: gameStationOf
      chessRepetitionEnPassant[$member] = -1
      if chessHistoryReset[$member] == 1 {
        chessHistoryLength[$member] = 0
        chessPositionCounts[$member] = 0
      }
    }

    // An en-passant target joins a position's identity only while some capture of it is legal: a pawn of the side to move
    // beside the victim on its rank, its king not attacked once the pawn leaves its square, the victim is taken and the
    // target is filled. No attacker but a slider moves with the capture (the victim is a pawn, read out of the pawns), so
    // only the sliders' rays are read again, over the occupancy after it (`boardSlide`), and the board is never copied.
    rule "tabletop-history-en-passant" {
      local turn = chessTurn[$member]
      local target = chessEnPassantTarget[$member]
      local sign = 1 - 2 * turn
      local victim = target - 8 * sign
      local kingMask = turn == TurnColor.White ? board(mask, chessBoard[$member], 6, 6) : board(mask, chessBoard[$member], -6, -6)
      local nearFiles = boardShift(kingMask, chessBoard0, E) | boardShift(kingMask, chessBoard0, W)
      local farFiles = (boardShift(nearFiles, chessBoard0, E) | boardShift(nearFiles, chessBoard0, W)) & ~(kingMask)
      local kingBand = kingMask | nearFiles
      local pawnFront = (
        turn == TurnColor.White ? boardShift(nearFiles, chessBoard0, S) : boardShift(nearFiles, chessBoard0, N)
      )
      local pawns = turn == TurnColor.White ? board(mask, chessBoard[$member], -1, -1) : board(mask, chessBoard[$member], 1, 1)
      local knights = turn == TurnColor.White ? board(mask, chessBoard[$member], -2, -2) : board(mask, chessBoard[$member], 2, 2)
      local kings = turn == TurnColor.White ? board(mask, chessBoard[$member], -6, -6) : board(mask, chessBoard[$member], 6, 6)
      local rooks = turn == TurnColor.White ? board(mask, chessBoard[$member], -5, -4) : board(mask, chessBoard[$member], 4, 5)
      local bishops = (
        turn == TurnColor.White ? board(mask, chessBoard[$member], -5, -5) | board(mask, chessBoard[$member], -3, -3) :
        board(mask, chessBoard[$member], 5, 5) | board(mask, chessBoard[$member], 3, 3)
      )
      local steadyCheck = (
        pawnFront & pawns & ~(1 << (victim & 63)) |
          (kingBand | boardShift(kingBand, chessBoard0, S) | boardShift(kingBand, chessBoard0, N)) & kings |
          (
            boardShift(boardShift(nearFiles, chessBoard0, S), chessBoard0, S) |
            boardShift(boardShift(nearFiles, chessBoard0, N), chessBoard0, N) |
            boardShift(farFiles, chessBoard0, S) |
            boardShift(farFiles, chessBoard0, N)
          ) & knights !=
        0
      )
      local after = ~(board(mask, chessBoard[$member], 0, 0)) & ~(1 << (victim & 63)) | 1 << target
      local afterWest = after & ~(1 << ((victim - 1) & 63))
      local afterEast = after & ~(1 << ((victim + 1) & 63))
      when chessHistoryPending[$member] == 1 and target >= 0
      forEach: gameStationOf
      if ((target / 8) == (turn == TurnColor.White ? 5 : 2) and
        chessBoard[$member][victim] == -(sign) and
        chessBoard[$member][target] == 0 and
        setBitCount(kingMask) == 1 and
        steadyCheck == 0 and
        (chessEnPassantFrom(victim - 1, afterWest) or chessEnPassantFrom(victim + 1, afterEast))) {
        chessRepetitionEnPassant[$member] = target
      }
    }

    // A position's key hashes its identity: four injective piece-code bitplanes, plus side to move, castling rights,
    // and an en-passant target only when a legal capture exists.
    rule "tabletop-board-history" {
      local planeA = board(mask, chessBoard[$member], -3, -2) | board(mask, chessBoard[$member], 1, 2) | board(mask, chessBoard[$member], 5, 6)
      local planeB = board(mask, chessBoard[$member], -5, -3) | board(mask, chessBoard[$member], 2, 5)
      local planeC = board(mask, chessBoard[$member], -4, 3)
      local planeD = board(mask, chessBoard[$member], 0, 6)
      local position = hash(planeA, planeB, planeC, planeD, chessTurn[$member] | chessCastleRights[$member] << 1 | chessRepetitionEnPassant[$member] + 1 << 5)
      when chessHistoryPending[$member] == 1
      forEach: gameStationOf
      chessHistoryLength[$member] += 1
      chessPositionCounts[$member][position] += 1
      chessRepetitionCount[$member] = chessPositionCounts[$member][position]
    }

    rule "tabletop-history-finish" {
      when chessHistoryPending[$member] == 1
      forEach: gameStationOf
      chessHistoryPending[$member] = 0
    }

    rule "tabletop-apply-illegal" {
      when (chessVerdict[$member] == 0 and
        chessMoveOf[$member].kind != MoveKind.Illegal and
        chessBoardMismatch[$member] == 0 and
        chessPromotionPendingOf[$member][0] == -1 and
        chessPromotionPendingOf[$member][1] == -1)
      forEach: gameStationOf
      chessIllegalCount[$member] += 1
    }
  }
}

// The computer opponent's evaluation and the revision that names the settled position its answer belongs to.
template chessComputer(settleTicks) {
  rule "chess-ai-evaluate" {
    when search(ply) > 0
    mode: Level
    forEach: gameStationOf
    chessAiEvaluation[$member] = (
      100 * (setBitCount(board(mask, chessBoard[$member], 1, 1)) - setBitCount(board(mask, chessBoard[$member], -1, -1))) +
      320 * (setBitCount(board(mask, chessBoard[$member], 2, 2)) - setBitCount(board(mask, chessBoard[$member], -2, -2))) +
      330 * (setBitCount(board(mask, chessBoard[$member], 3, 3)) - setBitCount(board(mask, chessBoard[$member], -3, -3))) +
      500 * (setBitCount(board(mask, chessBoard[$member], 4, 4)) - setBitCount(board(mask, chessBoard[$member], -4, -4))) +
      900 * (setBitCount(board(mask, chessBoard[$member], 5, 5)) - setBitCount(board(mask, chessBoard[$member], -5, -5))) +
      12 * (
        setBitCount(board(mask, chessBoard[$member], 1, 3) & 66229406269440) -
        setBitCount(board(mask, chessBoard[$member], -3, -1) & 66229406269440)
      ) +
      8 * (
        setBitCount(board(mask, chessBoard[$member], 1, 1) & 72057589742960640) -
        setBitCount(board(mask, chessBoard[$member], -1, -1) & 4294967040)
      )
    )
  }

  // The computer opponent: aiSide 1 (the default) plays Black, 0 plays White and -1 leaves both sides to people.
  // A completed answer belongs to exactly one settled physical position. Search
  // never moves bodies; the live apply path acts once, then lets physics settle
  // and the ordinary validator accept the resulting board.
  // Keep identity as well as geometry: exchanging two same-kind pieces still invalidates a token-indexed answer. A saved
  // piece packs square + 1 in seven bits and code + 6 above it; metadata also fits in one exact Int. Each piece's rule
  // reads only its own cells, so a move wakes the pieces it moved; the revision moves whenever either changes, and the
  // search runs only once the board has rested (`chess-ai-enable`).
  rule "chess-ai-revision" {
    local pieceState = chessPieceCellOf[$member][$each] + 1 | chessPieceCodeOf[$member][$each] + 6 << 7
    when pieceState != chessAiBeforeOf[$member][$each]
    mode: Level
    forEach: chessPieceCodeOf
    chessAiBeforeOf[$member][$each] = pieceState
    chessAiRevision[$member] += 1
  }
  rule "chess-ai-revision-metadata" {
    local metadata = (
      chessTurn[$member] |
      chessCastleRights[$member] << 1 |
      chessEnPassantTarget[$member] + 1 << 5 |
      chessHalfmoveClock[$member] << 12 |
      chessRepetitionCount[$member] << 20 |
      chessPreviousInCheckOf[$member][0] << 27 |
      chessPreviousInCheckOf[$member][1] << 28
    )
    when metadata != chessAiOf[$member].metadata
    mode: Level
    forEach: gameStationOf
    chessAiOf[$member].metadata = metadata
    chessAiRevision[$member] += 1
  }

  // The computer moves once the board has rested, the last arrangement was legal (or nothing moved), it is its turn,
  // nothing holds it off and the game has not reached a draw limit.
  rule "chess-ai-enable" {
    mode: Level
    forEach: gameStationOf
    chessAiEnabled[$member] = (
      (chessAiSide[$member] == chessTurn[$member]) and
      (chessHold[$member] == 0) and
      (chessRested[$member] == 1) and
      (chessSettleHold[$member] == settleTicks) and
      (chessGameStarted[$member] == 1) and
      (chessBoardCollisions[$member] == 0) and
      ((chessVerdict[$member] == 1) or (chessBoardChanged[$member] == 0)) and
      (chessHalfmoveClock[$member] < 150) and
      (chessRepetitionCount[$member] < 5)
    )
  }
}

// The move door: a computer answer or a `chessInputOf` request becomes one relocation of the pieces' cells, which
// the table then poses.
template chessMoveDoor(settleTicks) {
  rule "chess-ai-request" {
    when (chessAiEnabled[$member] == 1 and
      chessAiBestOf[$member].revision == chessAiRevision[$member] and
      chessAiBestOf[$member].token == reduce(position, chessPieceCellOf[$member])[$each] and
      chessAiBestOf[$member].to >= 0 and
      chessAiBestOf[$member].to < 64 and
      chessRested[$member] == 1)
    mode: Level
    forEach: chessPieceCodeOf
    // The answer names one token, so one binding at most matches it.
    maxFirings: 1
    chessAiOf[$member].from = chessPieceCellOf[$member][$each]
    chessAiOf[$member].to = chessAiBestOf[$member].to
    chessAiOf[$member].mover = chessPieceCodeOf[$member][$each]
    chessAiOf[$member].pending = 1
  }

  // A numeric move mailbox is the console's and replay's real move door. It joins the seated player's apply path:
  // captures, castling and promotion are placed by the chess-ai-relocate rules, then the ordinary settled-board judge decides.
  // Its physical resting read also keeps live mailbox inputs out of hypothetical search candidates.
  rule "chess-input-move" {
    when (chessInputOf[$member].request == 1 and
      chessInputOf[$member].from == chessPieceCellOf[$member][$each] and
      (chessPieceCodeOf[$member][$each] * (1 - 2 * chessTurn[$member])) > 0 and
      chessAiOf[$member].pending == 0 and
      chessSettleHold[$member] == settleTicks and
      chessRested[$member] == 1)
    mode: Level
    forEach: chessPieceCodeOf
    // A firing clears the request, which closes the gate for every later binding.
    maxFirings: 1
    chessAiOf[$member].from = chessInputOf[$member].from
    chessAiOf[$member].to = chessInputOf[$member].to
    chessAiOf[$member].mover = chessPieceCodeOf[$member][$each]
    chessAiOf[$member].pending = 1
    chessInputOf[$member].request = 0
    chessInputOf[$member].accepted += 1
  }

  // A relocation moves at most one piece each way: the piece taken on the target square (or en passant behind it), the
  // mover, and a castling rook. Each is one rule that fires for the one piece it names, in that order, so the capture
  // reads the target square before the mover lands on it.
  rule "chess-ai-relocate-capture" {
    when chessAiOf[$member].pending == 1 and chessPieceCellOf[$member][$each] == chessAiOf[$member].to
    mode: Level
    forEach: chessPieceCodeOf
    maxFirings: 1
    chessPieceCellOf[$member][$each] = -1
  }
  rule "chess-ai-relocate-move" {
    when chessAiOf[$member].pending == 1 and chessPieceCellOf[$member][$each] == chessAiOf[$member].from
    mode: Level
    forEach: chessPieceCodeOf
    maxFirings: 1
    chessPieceCellOf[$member][$each] = chessAiOf[$member].to
    if absolute(chessAiOf[$member].mover) == PieceKind.Pawn and (chessAiOf[$member].to / 8) == (chessTurn[$member] == TurnColor.White ? 7 : 0) {
      chessPieceCodeOf[$member][$each] = PieceKind.Queen * (1 - 2 * chessTurn[$member])
    }
  }
  rule "chess-ai-relocate-en-passant" {
    when chessAiOf[$member].pending == 1 and absolute(chessAiOf[$member].mover) == PieceKind.Pawn and chessAiOf[$member].to == chessEnPassantTarget[$member] and (chessAiOf[$member].from & 7) != (
        chessAiOf[$member].to & 7
      ) and chessPieceCellOf[$member][$each] == (chessAiOf[$member].to - 8 * (1 - 2 * chessTurn[$member]))
    mode: Level
    forEach: chessPieceCodeOf
    maxFirings: 1
    chessPieceCellOf[$member][$each] = -1
  }
  rule "chess-ai-relocate-castle" {
    when (chessAiOf[$member].pending == 1 and
      absolute(chessAiOf[$member].mover) == PieceKind.King and
      absolute(chessAiOf[$member].to - chessAiOf[$member].from) == 2 and
      chessPieceCellOf[$member][$each] == ((chessAiOf[$member].from & 56) + (chessAiOf[$member].to > chessAiOf[$member].from ? 7 : 0)))
    mode: Level
    forEach: chessPieceCodeOf
    maxFirings: 1
    chessPieceCellOf[$member][$each] = chessAiOf[$member].from + chessAiOf[$member].to >> 1
  }
}

// Closes a relocation once the table has posed it, and restarts the settle hold.
template chessMoveDone() {
  rule "chess-ai-finish" {
    when chessAiOf[$member].pending == 1
    mode: Level
    forEach: gameStationOf
    chessAiBestOf[$member].token = -1
    chessAiOf[$member].pending = 0
    chessAiEnabled[$member] = 0
    chessSettleHold[$member] = 0
  }
}

// The put-down path a move takes when a player makes it rather than the computer: the display door, through which a
// presentation of the game away from its board asks for a move (a game station's glass), and the capture of what the
// move is judged against. A seated player's put-down at a physical table sets `chessAiOf` and `chessPutDownOf.judging`
// itself, ahead of this template. A request waits while the board settles, a move is applied or judged, or something
// holds the doors off (a physical player's held piece among them, `chessGrip`), and lapses once its square holds no piece
// of the side to move or that side is the computer's.
template chessPutDown(settleTicks) {
  rule "chess-put" {
    local from = chessPutOf[$member].from
    local mover = chessBoard[$member][from]
    local ready = (
      chessHold[$member] == 0 and chessGrip[$member] == 0 and chessAiOf[$member].pending == 0 and chessPutDownOf[$member].judging == 0 and chessSettleHold[$member] == settleTicks
    )
    when chessPutOf[$member].request == 1
    mode: Level
    forEach: gameStationOf
    if (mover * (1 - 2 * chessTurn[$member])) <= 0 or chessAiSide[$member] == chessTurn[$member] {
      chessPutOf[$member].request = 0
    } else if ready {
      chessAiOf[$member].from = chessPutOf[$member].from
      chessAiOf[$member].to = chessPutOf[$member].to
      chessAiOf[$member].mover = mover
      chessAiOf[$member].pending = 1
      chessPutDownOf[$member].judging = 1
      chessPutOf[$member].request = 0
    }
  }

  // What the put-down is judged against, captured the tick it is made: every piece's square and code, each row copied
  // whole in one firing.
  rule "chess-put-before" {
    when chessPutDownOf[$member].judging == 1 and chessAiOf[$member].pending == 1
    mode: Level
    forEach: gameStationOf
    transform copyRow(row: chessPutBeforeOf[$member], from: chessPieceCellOf[$member])
    transform copyRow(row: chessPutBeforeCodeOf[$member], from: chessPieceCodeOf[$member])
  }
}

// The verdict on a put-down: an illegal arrangement is put back as it stood before it. Its codes are restored here, and
// with `restoresCells` its cells too (a drawn board, or a holodeck that then stands its bodies where the cells say).
template chessPutJudged(settleTicks, restoresCells = false) {
  rule "chess-play-judged" {
    when chessPutDownOf[$member].judging == 1 and chessAiOf[$member].pending == 0 and chessSettleHold[$member] == settleTicks
    mode: Level
    forEach: gameStationOf
    chessPutDownOf[$member].judging = 0
    chessPutDownOf[$member].revert = chessVerdict[$member] == 0
  }

  if restoresCells {
    rule "chess-play-revert-codes" {
      when chessPutDownOf[$member].revert == 1
      mode: Level
      forEach: gameStationOf
      transform copyRow(row: chessPieceCodeOf[$member], from: chessPutBeforeCodeOf[$member])
      transform copyRow(row: chessPieceCellOf[$member], from: chessPutBeforeOf[$member])
    }
  } else {
    rule "chess-play-revert-codes" {
      when chessPutDownOf[$member].revert == 1
      mode: Level
      forEach: gameStationOf
      transform copyRow(row: chessPieceCodeOf[$member], from: chessPutBeforeCodeOf[$member])
    }
  }
}

template chessPutSettled() {
  rule "chess-put-settled" {
    when chessPutDownOf[$member].revert == 1
    mode: Level
    forEach: gameStationOf
    chessPutDownOf[$member].revert = 0
  }
}

// The fresh-game door of a drawn board: a request sets every piece on its starting square with its starting code and
// the game's turn, rights, clocks and doors as they stood at the start, then the judge reads the board again as at boot
// (`chessGameStarted` 0 takes the starting position as the last legal one once the board has settled). It is a live door,
// never a candidate's, so the computer's search does not judge it. A physical table stands its own pieces back instead.
//
// It writes only what something reads before the judge's first settled pass recomputes it: the status line and the
// rings (the turn, a check, a draw limit, the last move), the doors and the computer (their requests, a relocation or
// put-down in flight, the enable bit), and the cells the next game carries forward (rights, the en-passant target, the
// clocks). The settled pass writes every other cell of the judge before anything reads it: the collision and
// mismatch counts, the candidate move's kind, mover and capture, the history's flags and length, the previous checks
// and the pending promotions; and a search answer belongs to the revision the moved pieces bump.
template chessFreshGame() {
  rule "chess-fresh" {
    when search(ply) == 0 and chessFreshOf[$member].request == 1
    mode: Level
    forEach: gameStationOf
    transform copyRow(row: chessPieceCodeOf[$member], from: chessPieceStartCodeOf[$member])
    transform copyRow(row: chessPieceCellOf[$member], from: chessPieceStartCellOf[$member])
    chessTurn[$member] = 0
    chessVerdict[$member] = 1
    chessCastleRights[$member] = 0
    chessEnPassantTarget[$member] = -1
    chessHalfmoveClock[$member] = 0
    chessRepetitionCount[$member] = 0
    chessGameStarted[$member] = 0
    chessSettleHold[$member] = 0
    chessIllegalCount[$member] = 0
    chessInCheckOf[$member][0] = 0
    chessInCheckOf[$member][1] = 0
    chessMoveOf[$member].from = -1
    chessMoveOf[$member].to = -1
    chessAiOf[$member].pending = 0
    chessAiEnabled[$member] = 0
    chessPutDownOf[$member].judging = 0
    chessPutOf[$member].request = 0
    chessInputOf[$member].request = 0
    chessFreshOf[$member].request = 0
  }
}
